🎯 Sample Coding Problems
1. Two-sum / Weighing pair
“Given an array of weights and a target weight, check if any two values equal the target.”
Classic two-pointer or hash map problem.

2. Add large integers (strings)
“Add two non-negative integers represented as strings (possibly with commas).”
interviewkickstart.com

Useful to simulate manual addition and handle edge cases—carries, different lengths, etc.

3. Longest common substring
“Given two strings, find the longest common substring.”
interviewkickstart.com

Often tackled with DP, suffix structures, or sliding windows.

4. Graph connectivity / Strongly connected components
“Check if a directed graph is strongly connected.”


Check reachability from each node via DFS/BFS.

5. Matrix jump game
“Given a binary matrix, find the shortest path from top-left to bottom-right, where you can jump up to k steps in any direction, avoiding 1s.”


A BFS + state management problem.

6. String addition + Fibonacci follow-up
Start by adding string numbers (possibly with commas), and extend to compute the nth Fibonacci number using that logic.
reddit.com

